The `perm` is the permission that's being modified. The `g` is the ghost state (RwPerms<T> in this case). Both are mutable variables in the ghost block.

The issue is that when I do `g.read_guard_token.tracked_borrow_left()`, I get a `&CountResource<...>` but `split` needs `&mut CountResource<...>`.

